Subject: CP-T1.13 the owner's apply hold beside the commit fence
Why: A caller's session runs on a connection of its own, lent the database's one write lock, while the owner holds what is committed from its machine and goes on ticking, voting and appending (Amphora replication.md, Decision (lane P6)); the hold is one more reason for the fence's range to wait, so the durability fence promises what it promised before

